# Desktop launcher

Session projection-cache schema failures are data-compatibility failures, not user-plugin suspects. Their recovery verdict outranks sticky skip and never recommends clearing original sessions. Loader application errors contribute package-name evidence, excluding the `cordis:include` wrapper.

Cold start opens the **launcher window only** (same Electron process). Do not call `dsh web` until after `checkUpdate()`. Newer formal GitHub release → ask; skip or no update → start desktop unless dest `sessions/` is empty and `~/.dsh` has importable data. Close launcher only when desktop ready + `quitAfterStart` + healthy full start (`lastStart.ok===true`, not sticky skip, not recovery launch). Start / plugin-tree failure → keep launcher and show home **Recovery Board** (full plugin list, attribution, per-plugin toggle, batch disable suspects) — the ONLY plugin-level recovery surface; the boot page keeps transient actions (retry / cancel auto-restart / download log) plus a「回启动器排查」bridge (`shell:open-launcher`, BOOT role lands on home tab) and never grows its own recovery copy. Clearing sticky skip on「启动桌面端」forces restart; forensics disable/enable aligns via `startHarness` (not `startDesktop`). Batch disable via `shell:disable-plugins`. `HarnessController.restart()` awaits any in-flight restart then always starts a fresh `replaceOperation`. Skip-user-plugins recovery must not ensure market/usage/session-search/dshbot (standalone plugin; `removeLegacyDshbotPreset` detachment only); desktop-install still required. Desktop-owned rows mount ONLY via `--patch` overlays: `desktop-install.patch.yml` and `desktop-dsh-im.patch.yml` on EVERY start (full + skip), `desktop-usage-panel.patch.yml` and `desktop-session-search.patch.yml` on full starts only. The profile `cordis.patch.yml` is purely user-owned — ensure strips legacy managed blocks (normalizing an emptied file back to `[]`; the CLI rejects non-array patch YAML) and never writes them back; never pass that file to `--patch` (the CLI still applies overlays under `--skip-user-plugins`). Strip + overlay write are atomic per start — CLI `insert` does not dedupe by id, a stale block next to the overlay double-mounts. `harnessSpawnPlan` quotes whitespace-bearing args under the Windows `.cmd` shell. Missing in-box `DESKTOP_PACKAGES` are runtime damage `buildLaunch` pre-flights with an actionable error; skip cannot fix them. Forensics flags such suspects (absent from the profile list) as `inBox`/`desktopRuntimeDamage` — the Recovery Board says「内置组件损坏」(reinstall / `setup:harness`) instead of offering disable, and this verdict outranks the sticky-skip banner. after-pack proves skip compose on the real packaged CLI (`check-skip-compose-contract.js`: dump-config skip+full rounds, user-layer canary, managed-block migration replay for install + dsh-im, exactly-one install row and exactly-one dsh-im row); launcher flags must stay in the CLI grammar prefix (args.ts-derived test in `dsh.test.js`).

Launcher uses official `--dsw-alias-*` and the official light/dark tables (`data-ds-dark-theme`). Do not paint Appearance wallpaper seeds onto the launcher. `--boot-*` stays on the main-window boot canvas. Marketplace / wallpaper gallery still must not open extra product windows.

Versions are desktop Setup.exe from non-draft GitHub Releases, not a `vendor/dsh` pin switch. 0.2.7 is formally released with the launcher in Setup; `/releases/latest` points at 0.2.7.

Update ask + download progress sit on a **visible** launcher (openLauncher before the prompt). A failed/incomplete update falls back to the launcher home —「启动桌面端」must keep working; never leave a hidden window-less process. Only packaged + installer-launched waits for app quit. `downloadFile` fails on body error/abort or a content-length mismatch and deletes the partial. `last-desktop-start.json` writers: `startDesktopFromLauncher`, boot `shell:restart`/`shell:retry-full-plugins`, and `restartWithCleanup` (menu/tray/plugin-align) — success `{ok:true}`, failure `{ok:false}`. Sticky-skip truth is `launcher-gate.stickySkipActive` (shared by ipc + HarnessController).

